.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
CPP-API: Abstract interface for logger implementations\&. \fBAssimp\fP provides a default implementation and uses it for almost all logging stuff ('\fBDefaultLogger\fP')\&. This class defines just basic logging behavior and is not of interest for you\&. Instead, take a look at #DefaultLogger\&. 
.SH "Member Enumeration Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "\fBenum\fP \fBAssimp::Logger::ErrorSeverity\fP"

.PP
Description for severity of a log message\&. Every \fBLogStream\fP has a bitwise combination of these flags\&. A \fBLogStream\fP doesn't receive any messages of a specific type if it doesn't specify the corresponding ErrorSeverity flag\&. 
.PP
\fBEnumerator\fP
.in +1c
.TP
\fB\fIDebugging \fP\fP
\fBDebug\fP log message\&. 
.TP
\fB\fIInfo \fP\fP
Info log message\&. 
.TP
\fB\fIWarn \fP\fP
Warn log message\&. 
.TP
\fB\fIErr \fP\fP
Error log message\&. 
.SS "\fBenum\fP \fBAssimp::Logger::LogSeverity\fP"

.PP
Log severity to describe the granularity of logging\&. 
.PP
\fBEnumerator\fP
.in +1c
.TP
\fB\fINORMAL \fP\fP
Normal granularity of logging\&. 
.TP
\fB\fIDEBUGGING \fP\fP
\fBDebug\fP messages will be logged, but not verbose debug messages\&. 
.TP
\fB\fIVERBOSE \fP\fP
All messages will be logged\&. 
